      "id": "add-tangents-afc4fd",
      "name": "AddTangents",
      "category": "TangentMirrorSolver",
      "signature": "AddTangents(Target, In Curve Editor, In Curve Id, In Keys)",
      "params": [
        {
          "name": "Target",
          "type": "FTangentMirrorSolver*"
        },
        {
          "name": "In Curve Editor",
          "type": "FCurveEditor&"
        },
        {
          "name": "In Curve Id",
          "type": "FCurveModelID&"
        },
        {
          "name": "In Keys",
          "type": "TConstArrayView<FKeyHandle>"
        }
      ],
      "returnType": "Bool",
      "docs": "Adds tangents that are be mirrored.\nInStartY and InMiddlePointY define two imaginary, x-axis aligned lines.\nAll keys must be between or on these two lines for the mirroring to work as expected.\n@param InCurveEditor Used to get and set tangent values\n@param InCurveId The curve that all keys lie on\n@param InKeys The keys whose tangents to recompute\n@return Whether any of the keys can be interpolated (only user specified tangents can be interpolated)."
    },
    {
      "id": "add-tangents-d65792",
      "name": "AddTangents",
      "category": "TangentMirrorSolver",
      "signature": "AddTangents<TProcessCallback>(Target, In Curve Editor, In Curve Id, In Keys, In Process Tangent Info)",
      "params": [
        {
          "name": "Target",
          "type": "FTangentMirrorSolver*"
        },
        {
          "name": "In Curve Editor",
          "type": "FCurveEditor&"
        },
        {
          "name": "In Curve Id",
          "type": "FCurveModelID&"
        },
        {
          "name": "In Keys",
          "type": "TConstArrayView<FKeyHandle>"
        },
        {
          "name": "In Process Tangent Info",
          "type": "TProcessCallback&&"
        }
      ],
      "returnType": "template<TProcessCallback> requires std::is_invocable_v<TProcessCallback,FMirrorableTangentInfo&> bool",
      "docs": "Version that allows you to do additional processing for the tangents.\nFor example,  you may want to compute falloff values for each key. In that case, you probably want to manually iterate CurveData and use the\nversion of RecomputeMirroringParallel that allows you to interpolate tangent values further."
    },
